  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 180d0828f9cf423459360235cd6922f2, type: 3}
  m_Name: Heart
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DeepVisionTutorialSO
  steps:
  - The canine heart is a four-chambered muscular organ located centrally within
    the thoracic cavity between the lungs. It continuously pumps blood throughout
    the pulmonary and systemic circulatory systems.
  - The right atrium and right ventricle receive deoxygenated blood from the body
    and pump it to the lungs through the pulmonary arteries for oxygenation.
  - The left atrium and left ventricle receive oxygenated blood from the lungs and
    generate high-pressure contractions that distribute blood throughout the body
    via the aorta.
  - Cardiac valves including the tricuspid, mitral, pulmonary, and aortic valves
    maintain one-directional blood flow and prevent backflow during each cardiac
    cycle.
  - The heart possesses an intrinsic electrical conduction system composed of the
    sinoatrial node, atrioventricular node, and Purkinje fibers. These structures
    coordinate rhythmic contraction and maintain efficient circulation.
